From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:43:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: Add Samsung S5K5E3 image sensor driver

Add a driver for the Samsung S5K5E3, a 5 megapixel raw Bayer sensor
with a 2-lane MIPI CSI-2 output.

The driver supports three modes from a 24 MHz input clock, all with
896 Mbps per lane:

  - 2576x1932, the full array, up to 30 fps
  - 1280x960, 2x2 binned, up to 60 fps
  - 640x480, 4x4 binned, up to 120 fps

with controls for exposure, analogue and digital gain, frame length,
flips and test patterns.

The analog setup table is Samsung's "Analog Global Setting" from
fimc-is-cis-5e3-setA.h in their GPL kernel sources for Exynos devices,
as are the binning settings of the 1280x960 mode. Those sources assume
a 26 MHz input clock: the PLL, link rate and clock dependent timing
values here are the ones the Galaxy Tab S3 (SM-T820) programs with
its 24 MHz clock.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
